The conclusion (the strictly-stronger version we discussed — construct OpEnvelope, call the old theorem):
∀ i : Fin trace.length, (envOf trace binding i).exec_eq
i.e. the exact old state_effect_via_channels conclusion, per row, with the envelope constructed from the trace.

Form A — right after P4 + P5 only (constructions + assembly; the residual threads NOT yet discharged). Everything balance-derivable is gone (the provider/table match comes from trace.balanced), but the framework residuals are still carried as hypotheses:
theorem zisk_compliant_of_accepted_trace
    (trace    : AcceptedTrace)                                   -- committed witness; .balanced = channel-balance trust
    (binding  : ProgramBinding trace)
    (h_decode : ∀ i, (envOf trace binding i).aeneasBridgeTrust)  -- #111  (SET ASIDE) — also carries the per-row coverage
    (h_memory : ∀ i, (envOf trace binding i).memoryTimelineConstructionEvidence)  -- #76
    (h_nextpc : ∀ i, NextPcMatches trace binding i)              -- #100
    : ∀ i, (envOf trace binding i).exec_eq

Form B — P4 + P5 and #76 + #100 also discharged, only aeneas left. Those two threads remove h_memory and h_nextpc (derived from the trace instead), leaving the clean minimal form:
theorem zisk_compliant_of_accepted_trace
    (trace    : AcceptedTrace)
    (binding  : ProgramBinding trace)
    (h_decode : ∀ i, (envOf trace binding i).aeneasBridgeTrust)  -- #111, the lone explicit residual
    : ∀ i, (envOf trace binding i).exec_eq
aeneasBridgeTrust does double duty here: it's the decode bridge and the per-row coverage (it's what says "row i is opcode X among the 55"). So setting aside aeneas, the theorem is essentially "committed trace + program binding + the decode bridge ⇒ full per-step compliance."

The irreducible trust baked in (not hypotheses you can remove — present in both forms):
- trace.balanced — the channel-balance / proof-system-soundness premise (the RHS trust; it's an assumed conjunct of AcceptedTrace, never discharged — that's by design).
- The Sail spec (the LHS) and the Lean kernel; plus inherited native_decide in a few load/M-ext closures (#75).
- The 55-op coverage limit: the 8 defect/gap ops (signed-M + FENCE) have no arm — out of scope, because the circuit can't support them.

Honest caveats:
1. This is the target, not the current c5e75899 — that one proves the weaker bus_effect-form and carries the residuals as the explicit RowConstructionData bundle. Reaching Form A needs the strictly-stronger refactor (construct OpEnvelope → call the old theorem); Form B additionally needs #76 and #100 landed.
2. #76 and #100 are real, hard threads (cross-row Mem timeline; cross-row PC). "Done with P4 and P5" gets you Form A; Form B is the prettier signature but requires those two discharges too.
3. So if you want the single cleanest statement of where this is headed: Form B — (trace) (binding) (decode-bridge) ⇒ ∀ step, compliance, over the 55 sound opcodes, with channel-balance + Sail + kernel as the documented external floor.

